; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; frostfang_reach.glacier   centre (440.0, -145.0)   120 x 90   x 380..500  z -190..-100
; GLACIER PASS — completely re-thought, purpose intact. It was a 60 x 20 corridor with six
; ice props alternated left and right: a slalom course, and the player could read the
; authoring from the first one. It is a pass now. Two twenty-six-metre walls close the
; north and south of the cell and the route is the ground between them; three spurs of
; differing size and reach come off those walls and none of them alternates regularly; two
; narrow crevasses cut across at 25-degree falloff, which is a slot you go around rather
; than a prop you walk past; and the floor rises eight metres from the southern entry
; before dropping into the saddle. The two pockets are still pockets and still go nowhere,
; but they are wider hollows in the ice rather than gaps between models. Movement weaves
; because the land weaves.

