; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; frostfang_reach.ancient_aerie   centre (330.0, -245.0)   140 x 110   x 260..400  z -300..-190
; THE ANCIENT AERIE — an aerie that is finally high. The cell is a massif: the ground rises
; eighteen metres from its southern edge to a levelled summit court at twenty, and
; the crescent of standing stones and the nest are up there. Three precipices are cut into
; it — fourteen metres west, sixteen east and eighteen off the north face directly behind
; the crescent — so the court stands on the edge of nothing on three sides and the vista is
; the reveal. The bent procession is now genuinely bent: it switchbacks west and then back
; east up the last eleven metres, because a straight line up that face would be a
; thirty-nine-degree ramp. The hidden hoard is a notch stepped a metre below the court
; behind the east horn, out of sight from the procession.

